ITEMS = ((('when should i call an ambulance', 'when do i need to call an ambulance when calling an ambulance', 'what situations require calling an ambulance', 'how can a person know when to call an ambulance', 'should i call an ambulance for an emergency', 'when is it right to call an ambulance', 'what counts as an ambulance emergency', 'how urgent does it need to be to call an ambulance', 'when to ring for an ambulance in first aid', 'what if i am unsure about calling an ambulance'), 'Call an ambulance when someone has a life-threatening injury or illness, such as trouble breathing, severe bleeding, a suspected stroke or heart attack, or a reduced level of consciousness. If you are unsure, call anyway and describe what you see; the operator will advise.'), (('what information should i give when calling an ambulance', 'what to say on the phone to an ambulance service', 'how to report an emergency to an ambulance', 'what details does the ambulance operator need', 'how to describe the location for an ambulance', 'what to tell the operator about the patient when calling an ambulance', 'should i give my name when calling an ambulance', 'what if i do not know the exact address when calling an ambulance', 'how to speak clearly on an ambulance call', 'what happens after calling an ambulance'), "Give the exact location first, then what has happened, how many people are affected and the person's condition. Stay on the line and answer the operator's questions. If you are not sure of the address, describe landmarks or nearby shops."), (('should i call an ambulance or drive to hospital', 'is it better to call an ambulance than drive', 'when to avoid driving someone to hospital when calling an ambulance', 'can a bystander take a patient instead of an ambulance', 'what if there is no ambulance available', 'should i call an ambulance for a minor injury', 'how to decide between ambulance and taxi', 'why call an ambulance rather than self transport', 'what if the person refuses an ambulance', 'who can decide about hospital transport when calling an ambulance'), 'Call an ambulance for severe symptoms because the crew can start treatment on the way and alert the hospital. Driving is only sensible for minor problems when the person is fully alert and can move safely. If in doubt, call and ask the operator.'), (('can i call an ambulance for a child', 'what to say when calling an ambulance for a baby', 'should i call an ambulance for a sick child', 'are there different questions for a child ambulance call', 'what if a child is not breathing when calling an ambulance', "how to give the child's age to the operator when calling an ambulance", 'should i stay with the child after calling', 'what if the child is unconscious when calling an ambulance', 'when to call an ambulance for a child fever', 'who can advise about a sick child by phone when calling an ambulance'), "Call an ambulance if a child is not breathing, is unconscious, has severe bleeding or is very unwell. Tell the operator the child's age and symptoms, and follow their instructions. Stay with the child and keep them warm while waiting for help."), (('how do i call an ambulance from a mobile phone', 'what number do i dial for an ambulance', 'can i call emergency services without credit', 'what if my phone has no signal when calling an ambulance', 'should i put the phone on speaker when calling an ambulance', 'how to use emergency call features', 'what if i cannot speak clearly on the phone when calling an ambulance', 'can i text for an ambulance', 'how to keep the line open after calling', 'who to ask for help with the phone when calling an ambulance'), "Use your phone's emergency number for an ambulance and give the location even if the call drops. Many networks allow emergency calls without credit, and some phones can share your position. Ask a bystander to call if you cannot speak clearly."), (('what happens after i call an ambulance when calling an ambulance', 'how long does an ambulance usually take', 'should i prepare anything before the ambulance arrives', 'what to do while waiting for an ambulance', 'will the ambulance crew call me back', 'how to guide the ambulance to the address', 'should i unlock the door for the ambulance', 'what if the address is hard to find when calling an ambulance', 'how to keep someone calm while waiting when calling an ambulance', 'who takes over after the ambulance arrives'), "After calling, stay with the person and continue first aid while waiting. Clear a path to the door, unlock it if safe, and send someone to meet the crew if the address is hard to find. Response times vary, so follow the operator's advice."), (('should i call an ambulance for a heart attack', 'when to call an ambulance for chest pain', 'what symptoms need an ambulance immediately', 'should i call an ambulance for a stroke', 'is breathing trouble a reason to call an ambulance', 'when to call an ambulance for severe bleeding', 'what if someone has had a fall and cannot move when calling an ambulance', 'should i call an ambulance for a seizure', 'when to call an ambulance for an allergic reaction', 'what injuries always need an ambulance'), 'Call an ambulance for chest pain, stroke signs, severe breathing difficulty, heavy bleeding, a serious fall or a severe allergic reaction. Early help can make a real difference. Describe the symptoms clearly and let the operator decide what is needed.'), (('can i call an ambulance for someone else', 'what if the person does not want an ambulance', 'should i call if a bystander says no', 'how to help when someone refuses help when calling an ambulance', 'can i call an ambulance anonymously', 'what if i am worried about calling unnecessarily', 'should i ask permission before calling', 'what to do if the person is confused when calling an ambulance', 'when to call despite objections', 'who decides if an ambulance is needed'), 'You can call an ambulance for someone else if you believe they are seriously ill or injured. If they refuse, explain your concern and call anyway if the condition is life-threatening. Tell the operator about the refusal and let them advise.'), (('what is the emergency number for an ambulance', 'how do i find the local ambulance number', 'does the ambulance number work from any phone', 'should i know the ambulance number abroad', 'what if i am in another country and need an ambulance', 'how to check the local emergency number when calling an ambulance', 'can i dial emergency services from a hotel when calling an ambulance', 'what if i cannot remember the number when calling an ambulance', 'who can tell me the local ambulance number', 'how to save emergency numbers in my phone when calling an ambulance'), 'Emergency numbers differ between countries, so check the local number when you travel and save it in your phone. In many places a single number connects you to all emergency services. Ask a local person or receptionist if you are unsure.'), (('what should i do while waiting for an ambulance to arrive', 'should i move the person before the ambulance comes', 'can i give food or drink while waiting when calling an ambulance', 'how to keep the scene safe when calling an ambulance', 'what if the person gets worse when calling an ambulance', 'should i take photos or notes for the crew when calling an ambulance', 'how to keep other people away when calling an ambulance', "what to do with the person's medication when calling an ambulance", 'when to call back for updates', 'who can take over first aid from me when calling an ambulance'), 'Keep the person as still and comfortable as you can and continue the first aid you have started. Do not give food or drink. Clear the area, watch for changes and tell the crew about any medicines or injuries when they arrive.'))
